  "notes": "After East wins the ♠A, and returns a spade, South's only possible loser is in the trump suit. South must avoid losing a trick to the ♥Q.\n\nSouth has 2 ways to play the heart suit worth considering. He could cash the ♥A and ♥K hoping for the ♥Q to be doubleton or singleton.\n\nAlternatively, South could cash the ♥A or ♥K (in case West has a singleton ♥Q), travel to the dummy, and finesse East for the ♥Q by leading North's hearts through East.\n\nThe correct play is to take the heart finesse after cashing either the ♥A or ♥K. A famous bridge saying, 8 ever, 9 never, can help you remember this play. When you have 8 cards between the two hands, missing just the Queen, finesse (as in this hand). When there are 9 cards between the 2 hands, play for the drop.",
